WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:05.460
There's a worthy successor to Game of Thrones
for your new medieval fantasy obsession, as

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:10.070
the Arthurian legend of the Lady of the Lake
gets an epic reimagining in Cursed.

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:14.680
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm revealing what the showrunners

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:19.240
left out from the ending of Cursed and how
it reveals the truth about Nimue's fate, plus

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:23.099
why some character deaths may not be what
they first seem.

00:00:23.099 --> 00:00:26.169
Spoilers ahead, of course, so take care if
you're not all caught up.

00:00:26.169 --> 00:00:30.859
At the end of Cursed the creepy religious
fanatic Iris shoots a pair of arrows into

00:00:30.859 --> 00:00:34.210
Nimue,
sending her plunging into the waterfall below,

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:37.120
but the big question is whether Nimue is dead
or alive.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:41.359
The ending was foreshadowed in the very first
episode when a deer was shot dead with an

00:00:41.359 --> 00:00:45.219
arrow right in front of Nimue,
and it was also foreshadowed in the many recurring

00:00:45.219 --> 00:00:49.160
visions she has of herself sinking into a
pool of bloody water with arrows stuck in

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:50.160
her body.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:54.010
But what's missing from the finale is a crucial
epilogue scene from the book on which the

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:58.510
Netflix show is based, in which we discover
that Nimue does indeed survive.

00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:01.260
The book by Tom Wheeler and Frank Miller reveals
that:

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:05.250
"Nimue's body washed up on a sandbar in the
shadows of [...] the Minotaur Mountains.

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:08.050
The arrow in her back had broken off to a
stump.

00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:10.330
The other arrows were bent under her weight.

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:12.610
Her breath came in heaving intervals."

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:16.861
And there are some subtle details in the TV
show that support the idea that Nimue will

00:01:16.861 --> 00:01:19.220
survive her fall into the water.

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:23.710
In the very final scene, Iris takes up her
new position in the Church's Trinity Guard,

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:27.590
but shots of Nimue sinking below the water
are rapidly cut in;

00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:32.680
and, crucially, gasping, breathing sounds
have been mixed into the audio and score at

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:33.680
this moment.

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:34.880
[gasping breaths]
[gasping breaths continue]

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:39.570
And if you pause on some of those flashes
you'll also see that Nimue's eyes have opened.

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:43.670
On top of that, mixed into Nimue's visions
are glimpses of her underwater but swimming

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:45.490
back up to the surface.

00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:49.470
The book also tells us what happens after
Nimue washes up on the shore:

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:51.190
"Something moved near her.

00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:53.640
Dozens of bodies swayed over Nimue.

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:56.910
Blistered hands, some missing fingers, pushed
and probed at her.

00:01:56.910 --> 00:02:00.980
the ghoulish hands reached underneath Nimue's
body and lifted her into the air.

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:06.390
The leper mob swarmed her limp body and spirited
it into a dark and foreboding tunnel."

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:10.860
The leper mob mentioned here are the gruesome
militia that serves Rugen, the Leper King,

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:14.890
and are the ones who came to take Merlin away
to meet the dark Shadow Lord.

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:19.130
If Nimue does end up captured by the Leper
King in the second season, then it's worth

00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:23.880
remembering that her father Merlin is now
Rugen's enemy after the wizard stole the Fey

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:26.000
Fire from his hall of treasures.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:31.070
So, how did Nimue survive a steep drop into
water with two arrows stuck in her?

00:02:31.070 --> 00:02:35.350
Well, regardless of whether she has the sword
or not, Nimue has access to some incredibly

00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:36.670
strong magic.

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:40.891
As a child she saved herself from certain
death when she was viciously attacked by a

00:02:40.891 --> 00:02:42.200
giant Demon Bear.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:46.071
Remember how her mother telepathically told
her to summon the help of the Hidden

00:02:46.071 --> 00:02:49.569
"Call to the Hidden to aid you.

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:50.720
Reach out to them.

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:51.720
Call them with your thoughts."

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:55.690
And with that power she was able to bring
down a huge rock to crush the giant bear's

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:56.690
skull.

00:02:56.690 --> 00:03:00.740
And as the first season progresses,
she moves from struggling to control her ability

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:03.910
when she's angry to being able to call on
it at will,

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:08.069
such as when she uses the woods to attack
a small army of Paladins that she draws into

00:03:08.069 --> 00:03:09.069
a trap.

00:03:09.069 --> 00:03:13.980
Although I fully expect Nimue to survive,
she may end up transformed into something

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:14.980
else by her drowning.

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:20.000
For a hint, let's examine Nimue's vision from
the fourth episode when she's almost drowned

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:21.530
by a Red Paladin.

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:25.910
In this premonition, after she sees herself
sinking into bloody water, there's a shot

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:31.060
of some bloody hands rising up to grab some
branches, and if you look very closely, these

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:34.720
hands even have little green shoots or foliage
growing on the fingers.

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:38.730
Is this Nimue dying and then rising again
in a different form?

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:43.560
In the first episode, just before the deer
is shot, Nimue hears a voice telling her

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:45.730
"Death is not the end, Fey Queen."

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:51.000
If Nimue is reborn after drowning, it seems
likely that she is now the Lady of the Lake,

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:55.790
the fabled enchantress who, in the original
legends, gifts Arthur the magical sword Excalibur.

00:03:55.790 --> 00:04:00.590
There's a big hint in the book that this is
what the writers may have in mind for the

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:01.590
series.

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:06.230
In the novel, as Nimue feels herself slipping
away under the cold water she thinks to herself,

00:04:06.230 --> 00:04:07.500
"This was my vision.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:09.270
I will keep the sword safe.

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:12.700
Neither the Church, nor Uther, nor Cumber
will have it.

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:15.190
The War of the Sword dies with me.

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:18.079
Until a true king rises to claim it."

00:04:18.079 --> 00:04:23.349
As for Gawain, well, he's another main character
who we shouldn't presume is actually permanently

00:04:23.349 --> 00:04:24.349
dead.

00:04:24.349 --> 00:04:28.159
When Nimue discovers he's died from the torture
inflicted on him by the Red Paladins,

00:04:28.159 --> 00:04:32.400
she cries out in grief at the loss of her
dear friend, unleashes an incredible amount

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:34.639
of power, then collapses.

00:04:34.639 --> 00:04:38.699
Spoiler alert for Avengers: Age of Ultron;
this moment reminds me of Scarlet Witch in

00:04:38.699 --> 00:04:41.020
that film after her brother dies.

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:46.160
Later in Cursed though, when the Paladins
come to cart off Nimue, look carefully because

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:49.639
there are now golden leaves and shoots that
have grown on his skin.

00:04:49.639 --> 00:04:54.020
And then a mass of green grass and leaves
grow up from the ground around him to encase

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:59.650
him, presumably to form some kind of protection
or cocoon until he is ready to be reborn.

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:04.810
In Cursed, Gawain is also known as the Green
Knight, and in some of the Arthurian myths,

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:06.189
the Green Knight is green-skinned.

00:05:06.189 --> 00:05:10.849
It'll be interesting to see if this is something
the showrunners plan for Gawain when he rises

00:05:10.849 --> 00:05:11.849
again.

00:05:11.849 --> 00:05:17.020
I think Gawain's revival will prove that Nimue
actually has the power to bestow life.

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:21.479
Remember that she was able to make a withered
old fruit tree grow an abundance of apples,

00:05:21.479 --> 00:05:25.130
and when Merlin asked her what she had done
to make this happen she told him,

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:26.389
"I thought about someone I love."

00:05:26.389 --> 00:05:30.370
Could Gawain be the person she was thinking
of platonically in that moment?

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:34.330
And perhaps because of the grief she felt
at losing him, she unknowingly brought him

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:37.130
back to life by wishing he hadn't died.

00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:41.620
And what if as Nimue was drowning she recalled
this advice from Merlin to draw upon the powers

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:42.620
of the Hidden?

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:44.539
"Imagine the result you want.

00:05:44.539 --> 00:05:48.160
Create an intention...
and then surrender that intention to the Hidden."

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:53.569
The idea of rebirth and transformation isn't
just limited to Nimue and Gawain in Cursed.

00:05:53.569 --> 00:05:58.610
For example, Morgana is infected by the Spider-God,
the Cailleach, when she meets a vision of

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:00.210
her dead girlfriend Celia.

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:05.039
Morgana then becomes a powerful sorceress
when she kills the deathly Widow and transforms

00:06:05.039 --> 00:06:06.419
into that character.

00:06:06.419 --> 00:06:11.680
In case you missed it, it happens during the
animated transition after Widow catches Morgana.

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:16.159
The sword first pierces the Widow and kills
her, but then the Widow's essence or spirit

00:06:16.159 --> 00:06:19.139
seems to enter Morgana and take her over.

00:06:19.139 --> 00:06:24.150
This moment completes Morgana's transformation
into Morgan le Fay, the powerful enchantress

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:26.090
from the Arthurian legends.

00:06:26.090 --> 00:06:31.099
The Weeping Monk also transforms from being
a weapon of evil and destruction for the Church

00:06:31.099 --> 00:06:35.800
and converts back to his original Fey nature,
taking back his real name, Lancelot.

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:41.619
Merlin too is renewed after picking up the
sword, going from a mortal and magicless trickster

00:06:41.619 --> 00:06:45.849
to finally getting his mojo back,
including some impressive lightning powers

00:06:45.849 --> 00:06:49.280
when he goes all Thor: Ragnarok on the Red
Paladins.

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:53.930
Squirrel has also graduated to the position
of a knight by proving his bravery to Gawain;

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:58.360
and with the reveal that his real name is
Percival, this sets him up to be the Grail

00:06:58.360 --> 00:07:00.229
Knight from the legends.

00:07:00.229 --> 00:07:05.039
There's also the diminutive but deadly Iris
who rises from the status of an ordinary nun

00:07:05.039 --> 00:07:09.560
who had to take orders from Sister Igraine,
to becoming a member of the Pope's fearsome

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:11.060
Trinity Guard.

00:07:11.060 --> 00:07:15.219
"Together, we shall accomplish great miracles,
my child."

00:07:15.219 --> 00:07:19.960
And let's not forget Arthur too, who begins
the show as a liar and thief who hangs around

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:24.199
with low-life mercenaries like Bors,
but he ends up as a leader and protector of

00:07:24.199 --> 00:07:27.759
the Fey people, even willing to sacrifice
himself for them.

00:07:27.759 --> 00:07:32.610
Arthur also saves Red Spear's life during
the battle with Cumber's army and the meeting

00:07:32.610 --> 00:07:35.580
between these two at the end sets up a future
storyline.

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:39.680
"I am the Red Spear, exile of the court of
Cumber the Ice King."

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:40.680
"I'm Arthur.

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:44.219
We'll do all in our power to help your people...
if you help save our queen."

00:07:44.219 --> 00:07:49.360
In the book, Red Spear introduces herself
to Arthur as Guinevere in this moment, something

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:51.110
that doesn't happen in the show.

00:07:51.110 --> 00:07:55.360
In the Arthurian legends, Guinevere is actually
Arthur's wife and queen,

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:59.529
so it'll be interesting to see if there will
be any hints at romance between Arthur and

00:07:59.529 --> 00:08:03.979
Red Spear next season, and how Nimue might
react to that if she finds out.

00:08:03.979 --> 00:08:07.029
So, what did you think of the first season
of Cursed?

00:08:07.029 --> 00:08:09.039
And which were your favourite moments and
characters?

00:08:09.039 --> 00:08:11.569
Let me know in the comments below!

